(Now we need to ensure that we have candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (goal 4). We'll assign operator before anything that requires it? Not needed for other goals except maybe for locking origin/destination? Those actions require candidate_operator_linked for the availability being locked. For origin_availability_alpha lock_origin_availability requires candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource. So we need operator linked to origin_availability_alpha as well? Wait lock_origin_availability precondition includes candidate_operator_linked ?origin_availability ?operator_resource. So we need to link operator to origin_availability_alpha as well. Similarly lock_destination_availability requires candidate_operator_linked ?destination_availability ?operator_resource. So we need operator linked to both origin and destination availabilities. However goal does not require operator linked to those; but we need it for locking. So we must assign operator to origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha as well. However we only have one operator resource driver_operator_alpha. Can we link same operator to multiple candidates? The assign_operator_resource action precondition requires candidate_prepared ?candidate and operator_available ?operator_resource. It does not check that the operator is not already linked to another candidate. So we can link same operator to multiple candidates as long as each candidate is prepared and operator is available (but after first link, operator_available becomes false because effect removes operator_available). So after linking to first candidate, operator becomes not available, preventing linking to second. However we could release operator after linking to first candidate (release_operator_resource) to make it available again. There is a release_operator_resource action (parameters ?candidate - candidate_entity ?operator_resource - operator_resource) with effect operator_available and not candidate_operator_linked. So we can link, then release, then link again.)
